            <td>4.1/5</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2 id="best-opensource-woocommerce">#1 — WooCommerce (Best Open-Source Shopify Alternative)</h2>
      <p>WooCommerce is the single best Shopify alternative for merchants who already run WordPress, want full ownership of every part of their store, or prioritize the lowest possible total cost of ownership above a fully managed hosting experience. Because WooCommerce runs as a WordPress plugin, content, products, blog, landing pages, and commerce checkout all share one theme, one CMS, and one domain — there is no subdomain SEO split or double-pay for two platforms. The extension ecosystem covers every commerce niche: WooCommerce Subscriptions, WooCommerce Bookings, multi-vendor marketplaces via Dokan or WC Vendors, Stripe payment links, EU VAT compliance, B2B price lists, and more.</p>
      <p>The trade-off is self-hosting. WooCommerce forces decisions on hosting, backups, security patching, plugin conflict resolution, page speed tuning, and payment gateway compliance that Shopify handles automatically. For teams without a WordPress-savvy owner or agency, the ops work negates the cost savings. If you can handle the WordPress side, WooCommerce undercuts Shopify's TCO every time.</p>
      <p>Full feature-by-feature: <a href="/reviews/shopify-vs-woocommerce/">Shopify vs WooCommerce</a> compares pricing, SEO, plugins, themes, and scaling head-to-head.</p>

      <div class="product-box">
        <h2>WooCommerce</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Full ownership &amp; no lock-in</strong> — GPL, self-host anywhere, export everything, migrate any time</li>
          <li><strong>One platform for content + commerce</strong> — WordPress blog, pages, CMS, and checkout on one domain</li>
          <li><strong>Lowest TCO</strong> — Core plugin free; year-1 cost ~$200–$1,500 for most stores vs Shopify's $500–$3,000+</li>
          <li><strong>100+ niche extensions</strong> — Subscriptions, B2B, marketplaces, bookings, EU VAT, and 100+ payment gateways</li>
          <li><strong>SEO ceiling</strong> — Rank Math Pro, Redirection, custom schema, caching, image optimization plugins</li>
        </ul>
        <!-- Affiliate CTA position reserved -->
        <a href="https://woocommerce.com" class="btn" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow sponsored">Get WooCommerce Free</a>
      </div>

      <h2 id="best-hosted-enterprise-bigcommerce">#2 — BigCommerce (Best Hosted Enterprise Alternative)</h2>
      <p>BigCommerce is the best hosted Shopify alternative for high-volume, B2B, and headless brands that do not want the operational work of WooCommerce but are unhappy with Shopify Plus pricing or Shopify's API and platform limits. BigCommerce ships native multi-storefronts per region/brand, native B2B quote and price list features, unlimited API calls on Enterprise, and lower credit card processing than Shopify Advanced for comparable GMV bands. For catalogs above ~$1M/yr with multi-storefront needs, BigCommerce is routinely the winning migration target.</p>
      <p>The trade-off is the app marketplace. BigCommerce's app ecosystem is materially smaller than Shopify's, so niche use cases (specific POS apps, specific marketing automation) often require custom API work. If you run a standard DTC store with no custom requirements, you are probably better off on Shopify Basic/Advanced than BigCommerce.</p>
      <p>Pairwise breakdown: <a href="/reviews/shopify-vs-bigcommerce/">Shopify vs BigCommerce</a> covers pricing, features, scaling, and Plus vs Enterprise plans.</p>

      <div class="product-box">
        <h2>BigCommerce</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Enterprise-grade hosted</strong> — Multi-storefront, B2B quotes, price lists, open SaaS APIs</li>
          <li><strong>Lower TCO vs Shopify Plus</strong> — 30–50% cheaper in year-1 for multi-million GMV stores</li>
          <li><strong>Unlimited products &amp; APIs</strong> — No SKU caps; Enterprise has unlimited API calls</li>
          <li><strong>Headless &amp; custom frontends</strong> — Stencil, Next.js, and SDKs for custom storefronts</li>
          <li><strong>SEO &amp; structured data</strong> — Flexible URLs, native microdata, blog + commerce on one domain</li>
        </ul>
        <!-- Affiliate CTA position reserved -->
        <a href="https://www.bigcommerce.com" class="btn" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow sponsored">Start BigCommerce Trial</a>
      </div>

      <h2 id="best-content-squarespace">#3 — Squarespace Commerce (Best Content-First Alternative)</h2>
      <p>Squarespace Commerce is the best Shopify alternative for content-led brands, editorial creators, and design-first businesses where the look and feel of the site is itself part of the product. Squarespace templates and the Fluid Engine editor are the best-in-class among hosted ecommerce platforms for non-designers — you can build a magazine-worthy store homepage without hiring a designer. Commerce features cover inventory, discounts, abandoned cart, gift cards, POS, Subscriptions, and sell-anywhere social channels for most merchants up to a few hundred SKUs.</p>
      <p>The trade-off is commerce depth. Squarespace Commerce is weaker than Shopify on multi-currency markets, Shopify-level app ecosystem, B2B features, and niche POS hardware integrations. If your catalog exceeds ~500 SKUs or you rely heavily on apps, Shopify or BigCommerce is a better fit; if your homepage and editorial pages sell the product, Squarespace wins.</p>
      <p>Head-to-head: <a href="/reviews/shopify-vs-squarespace/">Shopify vs Squarespace</a> reviews templates, design, pricing, and commerce feature gaps.</p>

      <div class="product-box">
        <h2>Squarespace Commerce</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Best-in-class templates</strong> — 100+ design award winners out of the box</li>
          <li><strong>Content + commerce unified</strong> — Blog, portfolio, landing pages, and store share a theme</li>
          <li><strong>Fluid Engine editor</strong> — Drag-and-drop that non-designers can actually use to build premium homepages</li>
          <li><strong>Subscriptions &amp; commerce basics</strong> — Abandoned cart, gift cards, discounting, native POS</li>
          <li><strong>No plugin maintenance</strong> — Fully managed, no updates, zero plugin conflicts</li>
        </ul>
        <!-- Affiliate CTA position reserved -->
        <a href="https://www.squarespace.com" class="btn" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow sponsored">Start Squarespace Free</a>
      </div>

      <h2 id="best-beginners-wix">#4 — Wix Ecommerce (Best for Beginners &amp; Creators)</h2>
      <p>Wix Ecommerce is the best Shopify alternative for solo creators, artists, and small-business beginners who have never run an online store and want a zero-learning-curve experience. Wix's drag-and-drop builder, AI-generated template starter (Wix ADI), built-in Blog, Bookings, Memberships, Forms, and fully managed hosting combine into the easiest single vendor to get live with. For 10–200 physical or digital products, Wix Business or Business VIP is often the fastest store you can ship in a weekend.</p>
      <p>The trade-off is platform ceilings. Wix stores above ~500 products, multi-region currency and tax, or B2B workflows start pushing the platform limits. Migrations off Wix (because design and templates are proprietary) require rebuilding the storefront. Pick Wix if your brand is a beginner creator with a small catalog; move to BigCommerce or WooCommerce later.</p>

      <div class="product-box">
        <h2>Wix Ecommerce</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Easiest onboarding</strong> — Wix ADI generates a starter store in minutes for absolute beginners</li>
          <li><strong>All-in-one creator platform</strong> — Store, blog, bookings, memberships, videos, invoicing on one plan</li>
          <li><strong>Fully managed</strong> — Hosting, SSL, CDN, backups, updates, and security handled</li>
          <li><strong>900+ templates</strong> — Niche designs for artists, photographers, food, services, and more</li>
          <li><strong>AI commerce tools</strong> — Product page AI writer, AI logo, AI product background</li>
        </ul>
        <!-- Affiliate CTA position reserved -->
        <a href="https://www.wix.com/ecommerce" class="btn" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow sponsored">Start Wix Free</a>
      </div>

      <h2 id="best-addsite-ecwid">#5 — Ecwid (Best Add-to-Existing-Site Alternative)</h2>
      <p>Ecwid by Lightspeed is the best Shopify alternative for merchants who already have an existing static, WordPress, Squarespace, Wix, or legacy CMS site and just need to add shopping cart functionality — without migrating or rebuilding the whole storefront. Ecwid is a hosted commerce widget that drops into any site via an embed code, WordPress plugin, or Squarespace block. Because the cart, checkout, and payments are hosted by Ecwid, site owners keep full control of their CMS while gaining a compliance-grade ecommerce stack.</p>
      <p>The trade-off is depth. Ecwid's merchant tooling and extension ecosystem are a fraction of Shopify or WooCommerce. Venture and Unlimited plans cover small and mid-sized stores, but brands heading past 10k SKUs or complex B2B workflows should migrate to WooCommerce or BigCommerce instead of building on Ecwid.</p>

